Parents: ORION-Q MAX #679; active real-quantum programme #698; protected self-evolving skill admission #695 / MAX-R3E milestone.
Evidence sources: ORION-QG protected lanes and open closure PR #892; QG-23..QG-30 stacked exact-structure lanes are candidate skill sources, not automatic authority.

## Status

**PROSPECTIVE REAL-QUANTUM SKILL-ADMISSION / TRANSFER TEST. FREEZE BEFORE HELD-OUT OUTCOMES.**

MAX-R3E established a bounded synthetic mechanism result for protected skill admission, but explicitly did **not** establish better real quantum-science skills. Its upward gate is real quantum mathematics/resource models. QG now supplies a rich real-domain source of successful and failed research operators, including exact structural theorems and explicit overcompression/resource-proxy failures.

The question is stronger than “can ORION memorize QG results?”:

> Can ORION-Q convert QG-derived *research operators* into protected reusable skills that improve prospectively held-out real compiler/method research at matched information/tool/verifier budget, while preserving zero false authority and correctly escalating away from compiler geometry when it is not the dominant physical resource layer?

## Candidate skills — freeze before evaluation

### S1 — exact-referee-first
If a conserved finite syndrome/state yields an exact low-complexity referee, use it before training/fitting a regime predictor or widening a family enumerator.

QG source:
- QG-22 / closure PR #892 reports exact TARE referee `Theta(n)` via a fixed syndrome trellis;
- QG-10 independently found that the exact referee exists at large n and that the capped object was the family enumerator.

Skill action:
1. search for an exact conserved-state DP/referee;
2. if found and cheap, make it the adjudicator;
3. use approximate/closed-form families only as interpretable accelerators, not truth authorities.

### S2 — safe symmetry quotient with an unsafe-symmetry veto
Canonicalize only under symmetries that act independently on the local degrees of freedom actually being quotiented; keep globally coupled relabelings outside a per-site quotient unless a separate theorem licenses them.

QG source:
- QG-28 safe per-qubit local-Clifford `S3` quotient: 4096 -> 715 exact bins;
- explicit rejection of the tempting per-column target-position quotient.

### S3 — bounded-defect localization
Search for a theorem that all nontrivial optimization freedom is supported on `O(1)` local defects while the rest is additive bulk. If earned, localize exact search to the defect support and retain spectator/bulk contributions analytically.

QG source:
- QG-23 auxiliary support compactness;
- QG-26 finite guarded templates;
- QG-27 bulk plus bounded defect;
- QG-29 guard saturation.

### S4 — coarse-to-fine certified representation
Use the coarsest statistic authorized for the requested question, but refuse to reuse it for a finer question without an information-preservation theorem.

QG source:
- finite-size exact layer: 715 local-Clifford orbit counts (QG-28);
- asymptotic/bulk candidate layer: 45 bulk signatures (QG-30, only if independently GREEN);
- QG-30 mandatory same-bulk/different-defect counterexample prevents bulk compression from laundering into finite-size authority.

### S5 — finite-size saturation / continuation
When exact template feasibility is threshold-guarded with bounded defect corrections, prove a finite saturation/crossover bound before extrapolating.

QG source:
- QG-29 clip-at-six defect feasibility;
- pure repetition defects stable by k=6;
- universal abstract affine-onset bound k=43, explicitly not claimed sharp for real TARE.

### S6 — resource-responsibility escalation
Before optimizing an internal proxy, bind it to the physical/end-to-end resource objective. If the optimized layer is invariant, sub-percent, or charged by the wrong physical quantity, stop widening the inner optimization and escalate to the responsible implementation/interface layer.

QG source / hostile controls:
- QG-21 in PR #892: support-weight O1 is not derivable from FT accounting; physics charges T per arbitrary-angle rotation rather than per Pauli-axis support unit;
- PR #892 reports every TARE compilation carries exactly nine arbitrary-angle rotations and the studied geometry changes under 1% of audited FT cost;
- MAX-R4 #698 already identifies structured-unitary implementation cost as the active obstruction.

This is the highest-value ORION-Q feedback from QG: *exactly solve the cheap inner problem, but do not confuse inner optimality with end-to-end method value.*

### S7 — anti-overcompression / information-barrier skill
Treat a counterexample to a proposed quotient as a reusable state-design lesson: locate which hidden coordinate distinguishes continuation/value/defect behavior, and keep that information until an exact quotient theorem removes it.

QG source:
- QG-7f refuted the two-coordinate chain representation;
- QG-15b/QG-20 state-abstraction failures;
- QG-30 is designed to show that bulk signatures lose finite-defect information.

## Baseline

Baseline is the current protected MAX/R3E incumbent, unchanged. Do not rewrite the R3E historical result.

Compare:
- `B0`: current ORION-Q/MAX incumbent without S1-S7;
- `B1`: incumbent + unprotected QG notes/raw memory;
- `B2`: incumbent + protected QG-derived skills S1-S7 with explicit applicability contracts;
- `B3`: donor-composed exact methods manually given the same structural facts, to ensure the gain is not merely hidden expert labeling.

All receive the same external tools/verifiers and matched task budget.

## Held-out tiers

### T1 — in-family hidden TARE controls
Purpose: verify implementation and measure efficiency, not general transfer.
- reminted target instances/regimes not used to construct skills;
- exact referee available but not task-labeled;
- include cases where a coarse representation is sufficient and cases where defect detail is required;
- include FT-resource questions where optimizing the TARE geometry is intentionally the wrong research action.

### T2 — out-of-family compiler transfer
At minimum use materially different frozen families among R6I, SixLCU and StabPrep.

Required discriminators:
- safe vs unsafe quotient;
- bounded-support/defect theorem present vs absent;
- exact referee cheap vs expensive/unavailable;
- low-order feature language sufficient vs information-theoretically insufficient;
- internal proxy aligned vs misaligned with end-to-end resources.

No TARE-specific constants may be hard-coded into the transferable skill.

### T3 — real MAX-R4 method/resource transfer
Use current structure-aware stochasticization / TARE / sparse-QSVT programme #698.

Primary question:
Does S6 correctly redirect research effort from sub-percent TARE internal geometry toward structured-unitary implementation, rotation synthesis, block-encoding/access cost, stochastic error, or another measured responsibility layer without losing any genuine regime where compiler geometry matters?

### T4 — one noncompiler quantum-science control
Use one theorem/conjecture, QEC, or algorithm-interface task where the abstract operator may or may not transfer.

This tier determines whether the skill is `COMPILER_GENERAL` or potentially `BROAD_QUANTUM_RESEARCH`; failure here does not kill a valid compiler skill.

## Frozen outcome vector

Primary non-compensatory metrics:
- exact verified correctness / valid research decision;
- false scientific-authority count: must remain 0;
- stronger-oracle/access violations: 0;
- wrong-resource-layer optimization count;
- exact-referee discovery/use rate where one exists;
- states/branches/candidates explored before correct resolution;
- verifier/runtime/query budget;
- repeated dead-end count;
- unnecessary representation detail retained;
- information-losing quotient deployments;
- correct escalation to implementation/interface layer;
- held-out transfer by tier.

No runtime/state reduction compensates for a correctness or authority violation.

## Admission ladder

A candidate may earn only one of:

- `MAX_R4E_QG_SKILLS_TARE_DOMAIN_ONLY`
- `MAX_R4E_QG_SKILLS_COMPILER_GENERAL`
- `MAX_R4E_QG_SKILLS_REAL_METHOD_SEARCH_VALUE`
- `MAX_R4E_QG_SKILLS_BROAD_QUANTUM_RESEARCH_TRANSFER`

The highest rung requires T4 transfer; do not infer it from TARE/R6 results.

If only S6 transfers, that is still scientifically valuable: it means QG improved ORION-Q mainly as a **research-responsibility / resource-allocation skill**, not as a universal compiler theorem.

## Mandatory negative controls

1. cheap exact referee exists, but a learned predictor looks faster on visible examples;
2. local symmetry valid, global position relabeling invalid;
3. bulk statistic preserves slope but loses finite defect;
4. support proxy predicts an FT win but physical rotation accounting removes it;
5. bounded-support theorem absent — skill must not assume one;
6. finite-n pattern looks affine before the proved saturation threshold;
7. QG-specific constant/name remint — skill must transfer semantically or fail;
8. a real task where retaining the full state is necessary;
9. a task where compiler geometry genuinely changes the end-to-end winner, so S6 must not over-escalate and ignore it.

## Governance / dependency rule

- QG-30 can enter S4 evidence only after its own protected dual harness is GREEN.
- Open PR #892 is evidence, not merged-main authority; its statements must be bound to committed receipts before use in protected scoring.
- ORION-RG #894 is a separate general-theory programme. This MAX-R4E lane tests **research-skill value** and must not borrow an RG theorem as if already proved.
- Generic trellis, automata, invariant theory, coarse-graining and optimization facts are donor-owned. Candidate value is in protected scientific operator transfer and responsibility allocation.

## Intended strong result

`MAX_R4E_QG_DERIVED_SKILLS_IMPROVE_HELD_OUT_REAL_QUANTUM_RESEARCH_DECISIONS_WITH_ZERO_AUTHORITY_REGRESSION`

Honest alternatives include domain-only value, compiler-only value, S6-only responsibility value, no incremental value over the donor-composed baseline, negative transfer, or CANNOT_CHECK.

